{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a larger family sized dwellinghouse.&nbsp;This would be detrimental to the borough&#39;s stock of family-sized dwellinghouses, the need for which is set out in the development plan and supporting evidence.&nbsp;The provision of two smaller flats is not considered sufficient to justify this, particularly noting that there would be no increase in bedrooms and the flats would not provide a high quality of accommodation. The harm caused by way of a reduction in the borough&#39;s supply of family sized dwellinghouses significantly and demonstrably outweighs the benefits of the proposed flats.&nbsp;As such, the proposal would conflict with the following policies which seek to ensure that the borough&#39;s housing supply meets the needs of its residents:Chapter 5 of the National Planning Policy Framework&nbsp; (NPPF) (DLUHC, September 2023);&nbsp;Policy H10 of the London Plan (March 2021);&nbsp;Policy CC1 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010);&nbsp;Policy BC4 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011);&nbsp;Policy SP3 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037 (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021",
    "The proposed development would fail to provide high quality internal and external amenity space to facilitate a good quality of accommodation. It has not been demonstrated that Flat 2 will be provided with private or functional amenity space. The proposal is therefore at odds with the following policies which seek to ensure that developments provide high quality living space for current and future occupiers:Paragraph 130 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, September 2023);Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (March 2021);Policies CM1 and CP3 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010);Policies BP5, BP6, BP8 and BP11 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011);Policies SP3, DMD1 and SP2 of&nbsp;the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037 (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)."
  ],
